page 90 (
    name: About
    alias: ABOUT
    title: About RESTaurant
    pageGroup: @administration
    appearance {
        pageMode: modalDialog
        dialogTemplate: @/modal-dialog
        templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    }
    dialog {
        width: 720
        chained: false
    }

    region about (
        name: About
        type: staticContent
        source {
            htmlCode:
                ```html
                <div class="rst-about">
                    <img src="#APP_FILES#icons/app-icon-192.png" alt="" width="72" height="72">
                    <div>
                        <h2>RESTaurant &APP_VERSION.</h2>
                        <p>An editor for the RESTful services of Oracle REST Data Services. It runs completely inside this application and works on the schema the application is installed for.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <h3>How the pieces fit together</h3>
                <dl class="rst-kv">
                    <dt>Module</dt><dd>Container of a service with a base path, for example <span class="rst-mono">/orders/v1/</span>.</dd>
                    <dt>Template</dt><dd>A URI pattern inside a module, for example <span class="rst-mono">orders/:id</span>.</dd>
                    <dt>Handler</dt><dd>The query or code that answers one HTTP method of a template.</dd>
                    <dt>Parameter</dt><dd>Maps a header, a URI value or the response to a bind variable of a handler.</dd>
                    <dt>Privilege</dt><dd>Protects modules and URL patterns. Callers need one of its roles.</dd>
                    <dt>Role</dt><dd>Granted to OAuth clients and users, assigned to privileges.</dd>
                    <dt>OAuth client</dt><dd>An application that calls protected services with an access token.</dd>
                </dl>
                <h3>Editor and compile check</h3>
                <p>The source editor is the Monaco editor that ships with APEX. The database checks the source of a handler while you type, without running it, and the first error is marked with its line and column. <em>Check Handlers</em> on the module pages checks all handlers at once.</p>
                <h3>Export and import</h3>
                <p>Modules, single templates and single handlers can be exported as JSON, as a SQL script or as a ZIP archive, and imported again in this or another schema. The JSON format is documented in the project repository, together with a JSON schema.</p>
                <p><a href="https://github.com/Hustenreizjuengling/RESTaurant" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/Hustenreizjuengling/RESTaurant</a></p>
                ```
        }
        layout {
            sequence: 10
            slot: contentBody
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/blank-with-attributes
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
        }
    )

)
